ers/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":1839,"digest":"sha256:a1922d1bf2d5573668a1360378ef883fac25526ad0057426b302f0d92eb47a90","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T00:55:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T00:55:30Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m128-v0.12.8/M12STAGE8-SHA256SUMS.txt"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/assets/757071727","id":757071727,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVj6ISs4tH_9v","name":"m12stage8-starter-manifest.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"enginsoysal","id":103884748,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjEnzA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103884748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal","html_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:f3fba5b947a78de15f10ab3eb176a6f5280d257231211ddf2d23b5d3b023c845","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T00:55:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T00:55:31Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m128-v0.12.8/m12stage8-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m128-v0.12.8","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m128-v0.12.8","body":"# Engacer OS M12.8 / 0.12.8 - Shared native file dialogs\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE8-VM-v1**.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/3aeb3751a2dfeddb886d44c4f86f46de47ac6aec/evidence/M12/8/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n587 compiled Git inputs and nineteen native scenarios. The exact VMware starter,\nseparate BIOS setup/ordinary starts, compressed-slot repair, compact light/dark,\nactual 150%/4K and twelve cached/full comparisons pass. Public delivery closes\nseparately before M12.9; see the [current delivery status](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/main/docs/roadmap/status.md).\n\nBuild: `9a36bb087f5db1ccbfc8510b72794654`.\nISO SHA256: `f4b4d7745782ce9414b8b46d24aba823348cf5a6fa92f06e48aae917a9f82c9a`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `a0a6bd436efd87c224b5fb193419c6004d096275c9d8941f0892abb83ecd0337`.\n\n## What changes\n\nText Editor Open/Save as, Image Viewer BMP Open, Archive Manager ZIP Open and\nChoose folder share real native navigation, file icons, extension filters,\nBack/Forward/Up, an editable location, personal places and New folder. A single\nclick selects; double-click or Enter opens. Ctrl+O and Ctrl+Shift+S are supported.\n\nCancel keeps the original document. Dirty Open has explicit Save/Discard/Back/\nCancel review. Existing targets need explicit replacement; changed, protected,\nin-use and failed-write targets cannot silently replace work. Extraction creates\na unique new subfolder at the chosen destination and retains the source ZIP.\nSuccessful choices remember separate Open/Save/folder locations in an optional\nversioned CRC-checked 792-byte per-user record. Cancel does not update it.\n\nThe dialog uses its existing owner even at eight live windows. Other windows\nremain usable. Their Open/Save as shortcuts cannot replace the active dialog or\nfall through to ordinary Save. Finish/cancel the dialog before display-size\nchanges. Invalid/oversized/binary text keeps the existing document.\n\n## How and why\n\nReuse the existing modal broker and shared visual controls instead of another\napp window, worker, framebuffer or growing queue. Source identity snapshots and\ncomplete checks precede commits. Checked text blocks reuse the volume scratch\npage and existing worker IPC input pages rather than an 8-KiB kernel payload\nbuffer. Generic Tab uses two bounded scans rather than reserving another 8-KiB\narray on every key. The guarded 16-KiB stack stays unchanged. Native ZIP/Enter\nand multi-page CPL3 text loading pass; failed prototypes remain in diagnostics.\n\n[Fixed and managed memory](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/3aeb3751a2dfeddb886d44c4f86f46de47ac6aec/evidence/M12/8/resources.json): fixed shell\nstate is 552085 bytes, 6449 above M12.7. Normal managed pages return from\n4288512 to the same number of bytes after closing; measured\npeak is 4583424 bytes across the multi-window tasks. No new\nkernel document payload buffer or per-window raster cache is allocated. Font\nbytes are unchanged. Configured VM RAM is not measured OS consumption.\n\n## Verification\n\nNative tasks check successful/cancelled saves, changed-target review, dirty work,\nfilters, real small binary/oversized sources, protected destinations and invalid\nnames. Every rejected choice leaves the complete owned disk unchanged. Actual\ninjected write faults and invalid preference clones keep work and their original\nbase disk. Independent GPT/metadata/data CRC reads match all stored documents\nand every extracted ZIP member. Tasks retain zero managed pages/new failures.\n\nFive display routes include compact 800x600 light/dark, 1920x1200/150% and\n3840x2160/200%. At 1280x1024 the existing global scale rule refuses 200% and keeps\n100% with an explanation; that is a refusal test, not a 200% or exact-minimum\nqualification. Idle CPUs halt. Individual compile-only stack frames supplement\nactual native tasks; they are not a complete worst-case stack proof or a human\nusability study. The host decoder passes 551 pages and 10808 malformed/fuzz cases.\n\n## Scope and retained limits\n\nUse the [matching eight-step installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/3aeb3751a2dfeddb886d44c4f86f46de47ac6aec/docs/handbook/install-m128.md)\nand [Open/Save/folder instructions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/3aeb3751a2dfeddb886d44c4f86f46de47ac6aec/docs/handbook/dialogs-m128.md). Source,\nevidence and twenty matching release assets remain tied to this candidate.\n\n- This is native app integration, not expanded Windows common-dialog compatibility.\n- Text remains supported ASCII up to 8191 bytes. Existing BMP/ZIP limits remain.\n- Copy USB files into native folders first; direct USB editing/replacement is unavailable.\n- Finish/cancel active transfers before opening a picker. Background conflict-review\n  arbitration remains an explicit M12.14 integration gate, alongside prior menu feedback.\n- Small startup modes versus explicit scale choices and cursor isolation remain M12.16.\n- The earlier concurrent BIOS/AHCI timeout remains open for M12.18; stress reliability\n  is not qualified. Final controller/original-app regression remains M12.18.\n- Physical/ARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal Windows support are not qualified.\n\n![Actual native Save as dialog](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/3aeb3751a2dfeddb886d44c4f86f46de47ac6aec/evidence/M12/8/feature.png)\n"}